      "id": "hellmark-flathead",
      "title": "Hellmark's guide to Ford's Flathead",
      "description": "Classic hop-up manual covering finned heads, multi-carb linkages, and cooling tips for Ford's 239 flathead V8.",
      "content": "Ford's 239 flathead V8 rewards patient hands and clean block passages. Scrub the water jackets thoroughly so both dual water pumps move coolant evenly, torque finned aluminum heads from the center studs outward, and re-torque them after the first heat cycle.\n\nSync progressive three-two-barrel carburetors so the center two-barrel carries crisp street response while the end carbs open together at full throttle, and set the front-mount distributor right on the timing mark.",
      "family": "ford-flathead",
      "parameter-name": "hp",
      "value": "3"
    },
