      "id": "hellmark-sbc",
      "title": "Hellmark's guide to Chevy's Small-Block",
      "description": "Shop manual covering valve lash, intake matching, and spark curves for GM's 265, 283, 327, and 350 small-block V8s.",
      "content": "GM's compact small-block V8 responds to careful assembly even before heavy machine work. Set rocker stud lash evenly across both banks with the engine warm so every valve opens to full cam lift without floating at the top of the quarter mile.\n\nMatch the intake manifold runners cleanly to the cylinder head ports, keep carburetor airflow close to 1.5 CFM per cubic inch across 265 through 350 cubic inches, and dial in spark advance with a timing light right on the balancer's sweet spot.",
      "family": "chevy-sbc",
      "parameter-name": "hp",
