      "id": "hellmark-windsor",
      "title": "Hellmark's guide to Ford's Windsor Small-Block",
      "description": "Street-and-strip tuning handbook for breathing, cam timing, and ignition setup on Ford's thin-wall 302 small-block V8.",
      "content": "Light, stiff, and eager to rev, the 302 Windsor thrives on clean airflow into and out of the heads. Torque the intake bolts in sequence from the center outward so the end seals stay oil-tight, and unshroud the air cleaner to feed a crisp four-barrel or multi-carb setup.\n\nWith the distributor mounted up front for easy reach, lock down the clamp only after checking full advance under the timing light and pair free-flowing headers with low-restriction mufflers to let the exhaust scavenge cleanly.",
      "family": "ford-windsor",
      "parameter-name": "hp",
