      "id": "hellmark-racing-slicks",
      "title": "Hellmark's guide to racing slicks",
      "description": "Trackside handbook on tire pressures, burnout heat cycles, and compound care for maximum racing-slick traction.",
      "content": "Soft-compound racing slicks make their bite through heat and a flat contact patch. Drop cold tire pressures until chalk across the tread wears evenly from shoulder to shoulder, and bring the rubber up to temperature with a clean, straight burnout before staging.\n\nBrush grit and rubber marbles off the tread between runs, store spare wheels out of direct sun so the sidewall stays supple, and inspect wear closely so a thin carcass never lets go at top speed.",
